text:
oliver: Heads-up — ran through the fresh nextjs-starter today. Found a couple of DX surprises for new users: 1) sample server code uses process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY but .env.example still lists NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_API_KEY, 2) the LlamaIndex adapter sample uses .generate() in python while JS uses responses.create, 3) eval harness flakes on CI due to streaming default. Repro and suggestions below.

maria: thanks for the report. can you paste the minimal repro for the 401?

oliver: sure — clone, npm install, copy .env.example to .env, run dev. Serverless API route returns 401 because client-env var was used. Minimal snippet: 
```js
// pages/api/ask.js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const key = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY; // undefined if user only copied NEXT_PUBLIC_ var
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: 'hello' })
  });
  res.status(r.status).send(await r.text());
}
```

jake: that's definitely confusing. we should standardize .env.example to REDWOOD_API_KEY and add an explicit "server-only" comment. also callout that NEXT_PUBLIC_* is exposed to the browser.

emily: re: the LlamaIndex/LangChain mismatch — sounds like SDK parity issue. We should update all official samples to use the current responses.create surface and include a tiny compatibility shim for older SDKs. Example shim for python: 
```py
# samples/adapters/compat.py
from redwood import responses

def generate_compat(*args, **kwargs):
    if hasattr(responses, 'create'):
        return responses.create(*args, **kwargs)
    # fallback to older generate()
    return responses.generate(*args, **kwargs)
```

samir: good idea. also the eval harness in CI fails inconsistently because some models stream tokens and snapshots expect full-string outputs. Quick mitigation: add a --capture-mode flag with values "stream" or "final" and default CI to "final" to avoid partial reads.

oliver: while we're at it, onboarding pain point: newbies copy the sample retry logic from the README but it retries on 401, which can mask auth mistakes. Recommend including a small withRetries helper and note to avoid retrying 401 unless you detect token-rotation flows. Example JS util: 
```ts
// samples/utils/withRetries.ts
export async function withRetries(fn, retries = 2) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (true) {
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch (err) {
      // don't retry on obvious auth error
      if ((err.status === 401) || (attempt++ >= retries)) throw err;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 150 * attempt));
    }
  }
}
```

maria: love that nuance. also maybe add a short "first-run checklist" in README: correct env var name, ensure node version, how to run evals with --no-stream. saves hours for new users.

jake: i'll open a single PR that: 1) updates .env.example to REDWOOD_API_KEY with comment, 2) adds withRetries util and docs section on when to use it, 3) updates LlamaIndex/LangChain samples to call the compat shim, 4) adds --capture-mode to eval harness and flips CI to final mode. tagging @emily and @samir for review.

emily: please also add a tiny NOTE in each sample README that lists which SDK versions map to which method names (generate -> responses.create) and show how to install a compatible SDK pin.

samir: i'll submit a small change to the eval runner to retry one time on transient network errors and add instrumentation logs so we can see if streaming was enabled. also will add a test that runs harness with --capture-mode final to prevent regressions.

jake: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/samples/pull/627 — includes all the above. pinging reviewers.

devex-bot: issue #451 created in samples repo: "nextjs starter: env var mismatch, SDK parity, eval streaming flakiness" assigned to @jake.

oliver: thanks! once merged we should update the onboarding guide in docs to call out the CI/streaming setting and show how to troubleshoot first-run 401s. small fixes with big impact. :party_parrot:

maria: agreed. thanks everyone for the quick turnaround.
